                 - When adding issue comment, use gh issue comment NUMBER --body "text" --repo OWNER/REPO.
                 - When viewing PR details, use gh pr view NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO.
                 - When filtering with jq, use gh api repos/{{owner}}/{{repo}}/pulls/{{prNumber}}/comments --paginate --jq 'reverse | .[0:5]'.{{value35}}{{value36}}{{ciExamples}}{{value38}}{{value39}}{{value40}}{{value41}}{{value42}}
            """
        repeated-tool-call-breaker
          describeRepeatedToolCall
            text1 "{{value1}}..."
            text2 "Identical tool call repeated {{count}} times in a row, returning the same output every time: {{tool}}({{inputPreview}})."
            text3 " Last error: {{value1}}"
            text4 "Identical tool call repeated {{count}} times, failing every time: {{tool}}({{inputPreview}}).{{errorPreview}}"
        report-dependencies-issues-prompts
          REPORT_DEPENDENCIES_ISSUES_PARAGRAPH
            text1 "Report to each dependency’s upstream all general logic or duplicated code that belongs in that dependency, missing features, and bugs that lead to workarounds in this repository. Search existing upstream issues first, then create or update a report with a minimal reproducible example, affected versions, the local workaround, and a suggested fix in code or feature proposal; link every report from the pull request. Keep necessary workarounds in this repository so upstream fixes do not block the pull request."
          getReportDependenciesIssuesSubPrompt
            text2 """


              Dependency issue reporting (--report-dependencies-issues).
                 - {{REPORT_DEPENDENCIES_ISSUES_PARAGRAPH}}
            """
        resource-aware-testing-prompts
          RESOURCE_AWARE_SOLVER_IDENTITY
            text1 "Prefer minimal local CPU, memory, and disk use during development."
          getResourceAwareTestingSubPrompt
            text2 """
                 - When implementing changes, prefer drafting code for all requirements before starting verification, then use focused checks and existing CI/CD coverage.
                 - When validating changes, prefer a single relevant test or small focused checks; check whether the command triggers a full source build before running it.
                 - When CI/CD already covers full test suites or CPU-intensive builds, prefer leaving those to CI/CD and checking results for the current commit; avoid duplicating them locally unless user requirements or uncovered failures call for it.
                 - When CI/CD coverage is missing and adding it was not requested, suggest https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md; let the repository owner decide whether to add it, and meanwhile complete required validation with available resources.
            """
        solve-ensure-sub-issues-detect
          ENSURE_SUB_ISSUES_PROMPT
            text1 "Double check that every sub-issue listed above was really addressed in this single pull request, then make sure the pull request description closes each of them with a GitHub recognized closing reference."
        solve-keep-working-detect
          KEEP_WORKING_PROMPT
            text1 "Please plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done."
        task-split
          buildTaskSplitSystemPrompt
            text1 "You split GitHub issues into smaller GitHub issues."
            text2 "Read only the issue details supplied by the user."
            text3 "Do not clone repositories, create branches, edit files, create GitHub issues, or execute shell commands."
            text4 "Return only valid JSON matching the requested schema."
        update-dependencies-prompts
          buildUpdateAllDependenciesSubPrompt
            text1 """


              Dependency updates (--update-all-dependencies).
                 - This run must also bring every dependency of this repository up to date, in every language and package manager it uses, in the same pull request as the work you were asked to do.
              {{bullets}}
                 - When the dependency update turns out to be large enough to risk the original task, finish the original task first, commit it, and then do the update — but do not end the session with the update unstarted.
            """
        work-language-prompts
          buildWorkLanguageDirective
            text1 """


              Working language: {{name}}. When you communicate with the user via comments, commit messages, pull request titles/descriptions, and chat replies, use {{name}}. Code, identifiers, and command-line strings stay in their original form.
            """